<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Pieterszoon Coen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Coen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Pieterszoon Coen was an officer and Governor-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in the early seventeenth century. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in 1619 as the company's headquarters. He also led the violent conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banda-islands">Banda Islands</a> in 1621 to secure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nutmeg">nutmeg</a> trade, a notorious episode in the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-pieterszoon-coen.jpg" alt="Jan Pieterszoon Coen" width="312" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques Waben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Pieterszoon_Coen_by_Jacob_Waben.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
